# Anchored HUD Overlays Implementation Checklist

Source proposal: [AnchoredHudOverlays.proposal.md](AnchoredHudOverlays.proposal.md)
Related feature: [project.todo](../project.todo), bow arrow type and quantity HUD indicator.
Planning requested: 2026-10-10. This checklist authorizes no implementation by itself; every task starts unchecked.

## Goal and execution rules
    Deliver reusable passive HUD overlays anchored to screen positions or named HUD elements, with bow ammunition as the first consumer.
    The proposal is authoritative. Its native API findings are prior evidence to recheck; its unverified runtime behavior is not a completion receipt.
    Use native ElementBounds and GuiComposer for bounds, alignment, and scaling. Keep feature policy outside the shared registry, host, scheduler, and layout components.
    Keep HudOverlaySystem client-only and thin. Follow the proposal's source responsibility directories; use one clearly named responsibility per file and directional dependencies.
    Document classes/methods with XML comments, explain nontrivial logic, and group methods by visibility and functional family. Avoid redundant forwarding methods and project staging language in production code/docs.
    Run all build/test tools through subagents, as required by the supplied AGENTS.md instructions. Do not launch the game; live acceptance is user-run.
    Before checking a phase complete, collect its focused evidence, perform a second review, and obtain an independent implementation audit against the linked proposal sections. Resolve and recheck findings first.
    Keep receipts in the existing validation workflow and concise checklist notes; do not create unrequested standalone audit documents.

## Scope boundaries
    Include internal registration, named anchors, dynamic group packing, scheduling, passive rendering, lifecycle/resource ownership, live configuration, and the base-bow indicator.
    Exclude interactive widgets, drag positioning, world/entity projection, automatic HUD discovery, collision avoidance across groups or unrelated UI, and a public cross-mod API.
    Exclude implementation of time/weather/temperature/storm features, migration of existing radial menus/progress or item-slot indicators, adaptive scheduling, new shaders/custom OpenGL machinery, a second UI bounds tree, an event bus, service locator, or global active singleton.
    Do not reserve smallblockgui positions. Native GetFreePos/OccupyPos/FreePos remain available for future conventional dialog placement; no replacement occupancy allocator is needed here.
    Keep placement preferences in VanillaExpandedConfig/ConfigLib. Native saved dialog positions are not a second position authority in this scope.
    Do not alter bow firing, reserve or move ammunition, mutate inventory, predict consumption, or introduce an arrow-selection preference.

## Assumptions and unresolved details
    Carry forward the proposal's defaults: both enable toggles true; hotbar-right attachment with left-middle group pivot and (12, 0) GUI-unit offset; vertical held-item-status packing; 12 GUI-unit safe inset; 1,000 ms default refresh; 100 ms heartbeat; 250 ms bow fallback refresh.
    Installed bow-selection agreement, actual draw ordering, supported event coverage, and live hotbar extent/visibility remain verification obligations.
    Gap, padding, cross-axis alignment defaults, concrete configuration keys/ranges beyond those named in the proposal, and exact internal signatures need implementation choices consistent with the proposal.
    The proposal transfers ownership of an overlay instance but also requires session rebinding after resource disposal. Resolve the reset/recreation contract before lifecycle consumers are implemented; retain stable registration identity and exactly-once final disposal.
    Confirm how supported screen attachment/pivot combinations map onto native EnumDialogArea and fixed offsets, including native margins. Do not silently replace native screen alignment with a parallel coordinate system.
    Future/replacement HUD compatibility and custom bow semantics are not established by the inspected base-game types. Missing anchors hide quietly; unverified custom bows remain unsupported unless a feature-specific adapter establishes their contract.

## Phase 1: Establish installed integration contracts
    Depends on: none.
    Proposal: [Existing foundations and evidence](AnchoredHudOverlays.proposal.md#existing-foundations-and-evidence), [Native positioning reuse](AnchoredHudOverlays.proposal.md#native-positioning-reuse), [Selection authority and compatibility](AnchoredHudOverlays.proposal.md#selection-authority-and-compatibility).
    Outcome: subsequent components can rely on concrete installed APIs without guessing behavior.

    ☐ Recheck the supported installed game assemblies and record their identity/version alongside the relevant method/type findings.
        ☐ Confirm HudElement transforms, GuiDialog opening/input contracts, UnregisterOnClose, and GuiManager.OnGuiClosed removal from both GUI collections.
        ☐ Confirm WindowBounds, ElementBounds scaling/alignment/parent-child behavior, render offsets, and the intended nine screen mappings.
        ☐ Confirm GetDialogBoundsInArea is an exact-alignment bounds query and returns an empty list for no matches; preserve its distinction from allocation and named-anchor selection.
        ☐ Confirm HudHotbar is discoverable through LoadedGuis and publicly exposes Composers["hotbar"].Bounds; verify the composer name and known element keys without depending on private fields.
        ☐ Establish a host DrawOrder below inventory dialogs, tooltips, and modal menus from installed behavior; leave actual appearance/input acceptance for Phase 7.
    ☐ Verify the installed ItemBow.GetNextArrow signature/accessibility and its use at interaction start and release; establish a cached read-only invocation path using existing dependencies.
        ☐ Verify EntityPlayer.WalkInventory ordering, opened-inventory membership, positive-stack eligibility, creative exclusions, and participation of opened external inventories.
        ☐ Identify usable SlotModified/open/close notifications, inventory membership changes, active-hand detection, and synchronized updates; document gaps covered by polling.
        ☐ Define the supported base-bow boundary from actual firing/selection behavior; do not infer compatibility from tags or EnumTool alone.
    ☐ Resolve the session reset/recreation contract, screen pivot mapping, and unspecified layout defaults within the proposal's stated ownership and positioning rules.
    ☐ Reconcile any installed mismatch or unresolved semantic conflict with the proposal before implementing the affected consumer; do not substitute a new selection or placement policy silently.
    ☐ Completion: installed contracts and remaining live-only questions are explicit, and second review/independent audit find no unresolved prerequisite for the dependent work.

## Phase 2: Define overlay registration and ownership
    Depends on: Phase 1.
    Proposal: [Ownership and registration](AnchoredHudOverlays.proposal.md#ownership-and-registration), [Proposed source responsibilities](AnchoredHudOverlays.proposal.md#proposed-source-responsibilities).
    Outcome: features can register bounded passive content without depending on each other or on native target details.

    ☐ Add the internal IHudOverlay contract under src/HudOverlays/Registration for applicability, refresh, stable sampled content, measurement, preparation, drawing, and lifecycle responsibilities.
        ☐ Support arbitrary bounded passive presentations; keep icon-and-text as a reusable consumer presentation rather than the universal content schema.
        ☐ Make the draw contract consume sampled/prepared state without gameplay queries, inventory traversal, or input handling.
    ☐ Add group definitions and overlay metadata: stable namespaced ID, overlay instance, enabled selector, group ID, order, and validated positive refresh interval with 1,000 ms default.
        ☐ Reject duplicate group IDs, duplicate overlay IDs, and unknown group references before changing registry state or taking resource ownership.
        ☐ Order by ascending numeric order then ordinal stable ID, independent of registration timing.
        ☐ Return an idempotent removal handle; transfer lifetime ownership only after successful registration, preserving caller ownership on rejection.
        ☐ Apply registry changes requested during iteration at the next pass boundary, on the client main thread.
    ☐ Define resource ownership and session rebinding according to Phase 1: final disposal once, session resources refreshed, borrowed engine/API/inventory resources never disposed by overlays.
    ☐ Add focused registry/ownership checks for rejected registrations, stable ordering, deferred mutations, removal during iteration, repeated removal/disposal, and session rebinding.
    ☐ Completion: registration and resource ownership are deterministic and verified; feature types do not leak into shared components; second review and independent audit pass.

## Phase 3: Implement native anchoring and group layout
    Depends on: Phases 1–2.
    Proposal: [Native positioning reuse](AnchoredHudOverlays.proposal.md#native-positioning-reuse), [Anchors and placement](AnchoredHudOverlays.proposal.md#anchors-and-placement).
    Outcome: registered content can be laid out using native bounds at screen or hotbar anchors.

    ☐ Add placement metadata and named-target resolution under src/HudOverlays/Anchoring.
        ☐ Resolve screen targets from WindowBounds with the 12 GUI-unit safe inset and native EnumDialogArea mappings.
        ☐ Resolve the complete hotbar composer through the verified public type/key; read renderX/renderY and OuterWidth/OuterHeight after composition.
        ☐ Treat hidden, closed, missing, uninitialized, or ambiguous targets as unavailable; hide dependents quietly and recover when available without fallback coordinates or automatic relocation.
        ☐ Read each required target once per visible host frame and share its result. Invalidate layout only when relevant bounds/availability change.
    ☐ Implement measurement, stable packing, attachment, viewport fit, and clipping policy under src/HudOverlays/Layout.
        ☐ Maintain one native root and child bounds per group/content hierarchy; use native relative helpers where suitable and explicitly repack after membership/measurement changes.
        ☐ Use native screen alignment; for named attachments apply groupOrigin = R.origin + A * R.size - P * S + g * O, with pixel-to-GUI-unit conversion before setting native fixed bounds.
        ☐ Preserve positive-X-right/positive-Y-down semantics, native render offsets, and exactly one application of GUI scale.
        ☐ Support horizontal/vertical packing, gap, padding, and cross-axis alignment; omit disabled/inapplicable entries and preserve remaining relative order when space closes up.
        ☐ Clamp the whole group within the safe rectangle while retaining member spacing; allow different groups to overlap without automatic collision handling.
        ☐ Retain the longest ordered prefix that fits; clip a single oversized first member instead of scaling it. Omitted entries remain update-eligible and recover when space permits.
        ☐ Invalidate on viewport/GUI-scale changes, native target changes, membership/order/placement changes, and measured content changes. Position-only changes must not rebuild presentation resources.
    ☐ Check native-bounds integration and geometry for nine screen mappings, differing pivots, offsets, scale changes, native margins/render offsets, multiple members/groups, hide/reappear, resize, clamping, and deterministic overflow.
    ☐ Completion: resulting native bounds satisfy proposal geometry and invalidation rules without a parallel UI tree or occupancy allocator; focused checks, second review, and independent audit pass.

## Phase 4: Add passive host, scheduling, and resource lifecycle
    Depends on: Phases 1–3.
    Proposal: [Update, visibility, and drawing](AnchoredHudOverlays.proposal.md#update-visibility-and-drawing), [Native positioning reuse](AnchoredHudOverlays.proposal.md#native-positioning-reuse).
    Outcome: registered overlays update and render through a reusable, passive native HUD host.

    ☐ Add HudOverlaySystem as client-only composition/event wiring and keep scheduler, native host, registry, and layout policy in their owning modules.
    ☐ Add the HudElement-derived host under src/HudOverlays/Rendering with one owned GuiComposer per group and native root/child bounds from Phase 3.
        ☐ Open without focus, return Focusable false, decline keyboard/mouse events, and capture neither general nor raw input.
        ☐ Use the verified native draw order and HUD transform; restore temporary drawing state through existing engine APIs.
        ☐ Draw only eligible group/content state and honor assigned clipping, including oversized content, without per-frame recomposition.
        ☐ Keep ordinary inventory dialogs from becoming an automatic hide condition; modal coverage follows native draw order.
    ☐ Add shared monotonic scheduling under src/HudOverlays/Updating with a 100 ms heartbeat, positive per-overlay intervals, and coalesced invalidation.
        ☐ Keep applicability checks cheap; perform expensive refresh only when enabled, applicable, globally visible, and attached to an available target.
        ☐ Publish stable snapshots; separate content/preparation dirtiness from measurement/layout dirtiness. Drawing must not sample gameplay state.
        ☐ Refresh before showing content after enabling, player/session replacement, target restoration, or HideGuis restoration; retain invalidation while expensive work is suspended.
        ☐ Continue bounded refreshes for overflow-suppressed entries; account for heartbeat granularity rather than promising exact sub-heartbeat latency.
    ☐ Add reusable icon-and-text presentation with native GUI item rendering and cached text resources.
        ☐ Render item presentation copies without mutating live inventory; borrow engine icons/atlas/meshes.
        ☐ Reprepare only for relevant content, locale, font, or GUI-scale changes; use accessible contrast, localization, and clipping/ellipsis within assigned bounds.
    ☐ Implement lifecycle and failure isolation.
        ☐ Hide for missing world/player, world exit, or HideGuis; support additional feature applicability restrictions.
        ☐ Set UnregisterOnClose true; use TryClose before disposal and TryOpen for reopening, without manually editing GUI collections.
        ☐ On LeaveWorld stop updates, detach feature subscriptions, close/dispose session host/composers, and clear session snapshots/resources/target references; recreate session bindings for the next ready world.
        ☐ Make final event/listener/resource cleanup idempotent and preserve borrowed-resource ownership.
        ☐ Hide a failing refresh/preparation consumer, emit a bounded diagnostic, and retry on its next scheduled refresh. Missing optional targets generate no warnings.
    ☐ Verify fake-clock scheduling and native host/lifecycle integration: coalescing, interval bounds, disabled/inapplicable/unavailable states, restoration, overflow updates, failure recovery, unchanged-frame resource reuse, and repeated session/open/close/dispose sequences.
    ☐ Completion: the generic runtime works with focused test consumers, passes relevant checks and second review/independent audit, and leaves live input/visual acceptance explicitly pending.

## Phase 5: Add the bow ammunition consumer
    Depends on: Phases 1–4.
    Proposal: [First consumer: bow ammunition](AnchoredHudOverlays.proposal.md#first-consumer-bow-ammunition), [Placement model](AnchoredHudOverlays.proposal.md#placement-model).
    Outcome: the supported active main-hand bow displays the next arrow type and total eligible quantity of that collectible type.

    ☐ Add feature-owned applicability, selector access, inventory sampling/subscriptions, and overlay content under src/BowAmmunition.
        ☐ Register vanillaexpanded:bow-ammunition in held-item-status with vertical packing and the proposed hotbar-right-middle / group-left-middle / (12, 0) placement.
        ☐ Hide for no supported active main-hand bow or a dead player; discard old snapshots when switching away or replacing player/session.
        ☐ Invoke the verified owning GetNextArrow method through a cached read-only binding. Keep custom-bow adapters feature-specific and hide unverified implementations.
        ☐ Sum positive stacks of the selected collectible identity through the same eligible WalkInventory traversal, excluding creative slots and other types; use a sufficiently wide accumulator.
        ☐ Preserve verified opened-external-inventory participation and engine ordering; do not group by stack-attribute equality or restrict traversal to a hand-written bag list.
        ☐ Display the selected icon and count; use localized names where applicable without an always-visible full name. Show a muted generic arrow and localized No arrows/0 state when a supported bow has no eligible ammunition.
    ☐ Attach/detach notifications across every inventory that can affect traversal; coalesce slot/open/close changes into refresh invalidation.
        ☐ Request 250 ms fallback refreshes while applicable, including inventory membership and active-hand checks; use available events to shorten latency without assuming complete event coverage.
        ☐ Reflect current client-visible synchronized inventory without predictive decrements or long-lived selected-slot references; selection may change again on firing release.
    ☐ Verify mixed arrow types and multiple stacks, including 12 + 8 flint alongside 30 copper producing flint 20 when flint is selected first.
        ☐ Cover zero/empty stacks, creative exclusion, external inventory open/close, traversal order changes, unsupported bows, no arrows, death/hand switches, synchronized consumption, and player/session replacement.
        ☐ Verify no inventory mutation and complete subscription/resource cleanup across enable/disable and world transitions.
    ☐ Completion: content matches verified installed selection semantics under focused checks, and second review/independent audit pass; user-run firing/display agreement remains a final acceptance requirement.

## Phase 6: Integrate live configuration and user documentation
    Depends on: Phases 2–5.
    Proposal: [Configuration](AnchoredHudOverlays.proposal.md#configuration), [Updates](AnchoredHudOverlays.proposal.md#updates).
    Outcome: users can enable overlays and select the held-item group's native screen or hotbar placement through existing settings.

    ☐ Extend VanillaExpandedConfig, existing ConfigLib mappings, and localization with a visibly grouped HUD Overlays section.
        ☐ Add EnableHudOverlays and EnableBowAmmunitionOverlay, both default true.
        ☐ Expose held-item-status placement as hotbar or one of nine screen positions plus X/Y GUI-unit offsets; retain packing/order settings as registration defaults.
        ☐ Use stable persisted keys and consistent defaults; unknown anchor keys revert to the group default, and nonfinite offsets revert to defaults.
    ☐ Implement ILiveConfigurable integration for settings and placement changes.
        ☐ Disabling a feature immediately stops its sampling and releases layout space; disabling all overlays stops expensive work while allowing restart-free re-enable.
        ☐ Apply placement changes through layout invalidation, with no unnecessary content resampling/resource recreation; refresh restored content before showing it.
        ☐ Keep config persistence authoritative; do not write duplicate positions through native saved-dialog APIs.
    ☐ Verify configuration loading, persisted key/ConfigLib display agreement, invalid values, toggles, screen/hotbar switching, offsets, and repeated live reload.
    ☐ Update appropriate user/developer documentation for settings, next-arrow/type-total meaning, missing-anchor behavior, unsupported bows, and ownership/registration expectations. Avoid claiming unperformed live acceptance.
    ☐ Completion: runtime/configuration/defaults/localization agree, relevant checks pass, and second review/independent audit find no integration gaps.

## Phase 7: Complete integrated validation and user-run acceptance
    Depends on: Phases 1–6.
    Proposal: [Validation required before implementation is considered complete](AnchoredHudOverlays.proposal.md#validation-required-before-implementation-is-considered-complete), [Approval decisions and remaining evidence](AnchoredHudOverlays.proposal.md#approval-decisions-and-remaining-evidence).
    Outcome: the implementation has appropriate automated evidence and explicit user acceptance of live behavior.

    ☐ Through subagents, run the relevant build and focused registry/layout/scheduler/lifecycle/bow/configuration checks; resolve failures and rerun affected checks.
    ☐ Inspect the normal build/package output for required configuration, localization, and presentation assets; keep package evidence distinct from in-game results.
    ☐ Reconcile the complete implementation against every linked proposal contract, including borrowed resources, subscriptions, native bounds/registration, supported compatibility boundaries, and absence of gameplay queries/resource recreation in unchanged draws.
    ☐ Collect user-run acceptance for normal/high GUI scale, window resizing, hotbar placement/extent, screen placements, HUD hiding/restoration, missing target recovery, and overflow behavior.
    ☐ Collect user-run input/render acceptance for movement, hotbar scrolling, bow draw/release, inventory interaction, Escape, dialogs/tooltips/modal menus, and representative third-party HUD layouts.
    ☐ Collect user-run ammunition acceptance for arrow-type transitions, synchronized consumption, relevant inventory open/close, no arrows, and world exit/rejoin.
    ☐ Confirm acceptable contrast, icon/count readability, hotbar-right placement, and refresh responsiveness; reconcile required tuning with the proposal and rerun affected validation.
    ☐ Remove temporary diagnostic instrumentation or scaffolding introduced during implementation; retain useful existing-workflow receipts without adding unnecessary audit files.
    ☐ Complete the final second review and independent implementation audit. Resolve every finding or record an explicitly approved deferral with its remaining acceptance boundary.
    ☐ Completion: source/API, automated, package, and live evidence are distinguished; all required acceptance is complete or explicitly approved for deferral, and no unsupported completion claim remains.

